 |\nL192: cite83†exam_coverage_tables.md | cite83†exam_coverage_tables.md |    |\nL193: cite84†exam_relative_coverage_tables.md | cite84†exam_relative_coverage_tables.md |    |\nL194: ## Repository files navigation\nL195: \nL196:   *   * cite85†README L197: \nL198: More items\nL199: \nL200: # ATTest\nL201: \nL202: A controllable CLI agent for generating and running tests for Python operators and APIs (such as PyTorch and TensorFlow) through a fixed, human-approved workflow.\nL203: \nL204: ## ✨ Key Features\nL205: \nL206: ### Dual-Mode Operation\nL207: \nL208:   * 🔧 Tool Mode (Chat): Ad hoc queries and file operations\nL209:   * 🔄 Workflow Mode: A 7-stage intelligent test generation pipeline\nL210: ### Workflow Highlights\nL211: \nL212:   * 7-stage pipeline: Function understanding → requirements generation → test plan design → code generation → test execution → result analysis → report generation\nL213:   * Smart feedback: Supports natural-language feedback and special commands (`/regenerate`, `/goto`, `/retry`)\nL214:   * Persistent state: Supports interruption recovery, with versioned artifact management\nL215:   * Custom execution: Configurable pytest commands, environment variables, and dependency installation\nL216: \nL217: * * *\nL218: ## 🚀 Quick Start\nL219: \nL220: ### Installation\nL221: \nL222:     cd ATTest\nL223:     pip install -e .\nL224: \nL225: ### Basic Usage\nL226: \nL227: #### Chat Mode (Ad Hoc Tasks)\nL228: \nL229:     attest chat --workspace ~/my-project\nL230: #### Workflow Mode (Full Test Generation)\nL231: \nL232:     # Interactive mode (recommended)\nL233:     attest run -f torch.nn.functional.relu --workspace ./my-project/torch.nn.functional.relu\nL234: \nL235:     # Fully automatic mode\nL236:     attest run -f torch.add --mode full-auto --workspace ./my-project/torch.add\nL237: \nL238:     # Fully automatic mode with multi-round iteration (3 rounds)\nL239:     attest run -f torch.add --mode full-auto --epoch 3\nL240: \nL241:     # Specify the project root when it differs from workspace\nL242:     attest run -f torch.add --workspace ./my-project --project-root ./my-project/src\nL243: \nL244:     # Resume an interrupted workflow\nL245:     attest run -f torch.add --resume\nL246: * * *\nL247: ## 📖 Documentation\nL248: \nL249:   * cite86†WORKFLOW_GUIDE.md - Complete usage guide (recommended)\nL250: \nL251:     * Detailed workflow mode walkthrough\nL252:     * Custom build command configuration\nL253:     * Testing and debugging\nL254:     * Extension and customization\nL255:   * cite79†QUICK_REFERENCE.md - Quick reference card\nL256: \nL257:     * Common command cheat sheet\nL258:     * Workflow interactive commands\nL259:     * Configuration examples\nL260:   * cite81†USAGE.md - Chat mode usage guide\nL261: \nL262: * * *\nL263: ## 🎯 Workflow Stages\nL264: \nL265:     `╔═══════════════════════════════════════════════════╗\nL266:     ║   ATTest Workflow - torch.add (python)           ║\nL267:     ╠═══════════════════════════════════════════════════╣\nL268:     ║ [●] 1. Understand Function                       ║\nL269:     ║ [●] 2. Generate Requirements                     ║\nL270:     ║ [▶] 3. Design Test Plan        ← Current Stage   ║\nL271:     ║ [ ] 4. Generate Code                             ║\nL272:     ║ [ ] 5. Execute Tests                             ║\nL273:     ║ [ ] 6. Analyze Results                           ║\nL274:     ║ [ ] 7. Generate Report                           ║\nL275:     ╚═══════════════════════════════════════════════════╝\nL276:     `\nL277: After each stage completes, you can:\nL278: \nL279:   * Press `Enter` to continue\nL280:   * Use `/regenerate` to regenerate the current stage\nL281:   * Use `/goto <stage>` to jump to another stage\nL282:   * Provide natural-language feedback for smart interpretation\nL283: \nL284: * * *\nL285: ## 🔧 Custom Build Commands\nL286: When you need to adjust the pytest command or environment variables, edit `~/.attest_cli/config.json`:\nL287: \nL288:     {\nL289:       \"api\": {\nL290:         \"model\": \"deepseek-chat\",\nL291:         \"base_url\": \"https://api.deepseek.com/v1\",\nL292:         \"api_key\": \"your-api-key\",\nL293:         \"temperature\": 0.2,\nL294:         \"max_tokens\": 4096\nL295:       },\nL296:       \"preferences\": {\nL297:         \"auto_approve\": false\nL298:       },\nL299:       \"project\": {\nL300:         \"root\": \".\",\nL301:         \"test_file_template\": \"tests/test_{target_slug}.py\",\nL302:         \"build_dir\": \"\",\nL303:         \"output_binary_template\": \"\"\nL304:       },\nL305:       \"commands\": {\nL306:         \"compile\": \"\",\nL307:         \"install\": \"\",\nL308:         \"run_test\": \"PYTHONPATH={project_root}:$PYTHONPATH pytest -q {test_file_path}\"\nL309:       }\nL310:     }\nL311: Available variables:\nL312: \nL313:   * `{target}` / `{target_slug}` - Target function FQN and its slug\nL314:   * `{project_root}` - Project root directory\nL315:   * `{test_file_path}` - Generated pytest file path\nL316: \nL317: See cite87†WORKFLOW_GUIDE.md - Custom Build Commands for details.\nL318: \nL319: * * *\nL320: ## 📋 Command Reference\nL321: \nL322: ### Configuration Management\nL323: \nL324:     attest config list              # Show all configuration values\nL325:     attest config set KEY VALUE     # Set a configuration value\nL326:     attest config get KEY           # Get a configuration value\nL327: \nL328: ### Session Management\nL329: \nL330:     attest sessions list            # List all sessions\nL331:     attest sessions clear ID        # Clear a specific session\nL332: \nL333: ### Chat Mode\nL334: \nL335:     attest chat [--workspace DIR] [--auto-approve]\nL336: ### Workflow Mode\nL337: \nL338:     attest run -f package.module:function \\\nL339:       [--workspace DIR] \\\nL340:       [--project-root DIR] \\\nL341:       [--mode interactive|full-auto] \\\nL342:       [--epoch N] \\\nL343:       [--resume]\nL344: \nL345: Arguments:\nL346:   * `-f, --func`: Fully qualified target function name (required)\nL347:   * `--workspace`: Working directory, defaults to the current directory\nL348:   * `--project-root`: Project root directory, defaults to the same value as `workspace`\nL349:   * `--mode`: Run mode, either `interactive` or `full-auto`, defaults to `interactive`\nL350:   * `--epoch`: Number of iteration rounds in full-auto mode; after `analyze_results`, the workflow loops back to `generate_code`; defaults to `1`\nL351:   * `--resume`: Resume an interrupted workflow\nL352: * * *\nL353: ## 🛠️ Extension and Customization\nL354: \nL355: ### Add a New Tool\nL356: \nL357:   1. Create a tool class in `src/attest_cli/tools/builtin.py`\nL358:   2. Register it in `src/attest_cli/tools/runner.py`\nL359:   3. Add it to a stage's `tools` list\nL360: \nL361: ### Modify a Stage Prompt\nL362: \nL363: Edit the corresponding stage file, for example `src/attest_cli/workflow/stages/requirements.py`, and update `_get_prompt_template()`.\nL364: ### Add a New Stage\nL365: \nL366:   1. Create `src/attest_cli/workflow/stages/your_stage.py`\nL367:   2. Register it in `stages/__init__.py`\nL368:   3. Add it to `STAGE_NAMES` in `workflow/engine.py`\nL369: \nL370: See cite88†WORKFLOW_GUIDE.md - Extension and Customization for details.\nL371: \nL372: * * *\nL373: ## 📂 Project Structure\nL374: \nL375:     `ATTest/\nL376:     ├── src/attest_cli/\nL377:     │   ├── cli.py                    # CLI entry point\nL378:     │   ├── config.py                 # Configuration management\nL379:     │   ├── llm.py                    # LLM client\nL380:     │   ├── session.py                # Session management\nL381:     │   ├── chat.py                   # Chat mode\nL382:     │   ├── tools/                    # Tool system\nL383:     │   │   ├── base.py\nL384:     │   │   ├── builtin.py\nL385:     │   │   └── runner.py\nL386:     │   └── workflow/                 # Workflow engine\nL387:     │       ├── engine.py             # Main controller\nL388:     │       ├── state.py              # State management\nL389:     │       ├── stage.py              # Stage base class\nL390:     │       ├── supervisor.py         # Feedback interpretation\nL391:     │       ├── display.py            # Progress display\nL392:     │       └── stages/               # Individual stages\nL393:     │           ├── understand.py\nL394:     │           ├── requirements.py\nL395:     │           ├── planning.py\nL396:     │           ├── codegen.py\nL397:     │           ├── execution.py\nL398:     │           ├── analysis.py\nL399:     │           └── report.py\nL400:     ├── WORKFLOW_GUIDE.md             # Complete usage guide\nL401:     ├── QUICK_REFERENCE.md            # Quick reference\nL402:     └── USAGE.md                      # Chat mode guide\nL403:     `\nL404: * * *\nL405: ## 🧪 Tests\nL406: \nL407:     # Test the core framework\nL408:     python test_milestone1.py\nL409: \nL410:     # Test custom commands\nL411:     python test_custom_commands.py\nL412: \nL413: * * *\nL414: \nL415: ## 📝 Examples\nL416: \nL417: ### Fully Automatic Workflow for a PyTorch Operator\nL418: \nL419:     attest run -f torch.add --workspace ~/my-project --mode full-auto\nL420: \nL421: Automatically generates pytest cases, executes them, and produces a test report.\nL422: ### Workflow with a Custom Pytest Command\nL423: \nL424:     attest config set commands.run_test \"PYTHONPATH={project_root}:$PYTHONPATH pytest -q {test_file_path} -k gpu\"\nL425:     attest run -f torch.add --workspace ~/my-project --mode full-auto\nL426: \nL427: Uses a custom command to run the generated tests, which can be reused in a virtual environment or CI pipeline.\nL428: \nL429: ### Quick Checks in Chat Mode\nL430: \nL431:     attest chat --workspace ~/my-project\nL432: \nL433: Temporarily inspect or analyze files, or generate small testing snippets.\nL434: \nL435: * * *\nL436: ## 🤝 Contributing\nL437: \nL438: Contributions are welcome. Main extension points include:\nL439: \nL440:   * New tools (file operations, analysis utilities, and so on)\nL441:   * New workflow stages (performance testing, coverage analysis, and so on)\nL442:   * Improved prompt templates\nL443:   * Better error handling\nL444: \nL445: * * *\nL446: \nL447: ## 📄 License\nL448: \nL449: MIT\nL450: \nL451: * * *\nL452: ## 🙏 Acknowledgements\nL453: \nL454: Inspired by:\nL455: \nL456:   * CliAgent - Flow-first design\nL457:   * Cougar-CLI - Config and session management\nL458:   * mini-kode - Permission-aware tool execution\nL459: \nL460: * * *\nL461: \nL462: Quick start: See cite86†WORKFLOW_GUIDE.md for detailed usage.\nL463: \nL464: ## About\nL465: \nL466: No description, website, or topics provided.\nL467: \nL468: ### Resources\nL469: \nL470: cite71†Readme L471: \nL472: cite72†Activity L473: \nL474: cite73†Custom properties L475: \nL476: ### Stars\nL477: \nL478: 3 stars\nL479: \nL480: ### Watchers\nL481: \nL482: 0 watching\nL483: \nL484: ### Forks\nL485: \nL486: cite74†0 forks L487: \nL488: cite75†Report repository L489: \nL490: ## Releases\nL491: \nL492: ## Packages\nL493: \nL494: ## Contributors\nL495: ## Languages\nL496: \nL497: You can’t perform that action at this time.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nGitHub - NVlabs/KernelBlaster: A framework for in context learning for code optimization · GitHub (https://github.com/NVlabs/KernelBlaster)\nciteturn31906view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://github.com/NVlabs/KernelBlaster\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 416\nL0: cite0†Skip to content L1: ## Navigation Menu\nL2: \nL3: cite1†Sign in L4: \nL5: Appearance settings\nL6: \nL7:   * Platform\nL8: \nL9:     * AI CODE CREATION\nL10:       * cite2†GitHub CopilotWrite better code with AI L11:       * cite3†GitHub Copilot appDirect agents from issue to merge L12:       * cite4†MCP 